# A root's result is what its World hears after each tick (Semantics ch. 7, "The outputs":
# the root's result), one value; a bundle is not data (Type System ch. 2, "Bundles and
# sparse tuples"), so a root cannot end on one. prismc's back end refuses it today ("a
# bundle as the root's result"); the checker should. Written by Claude on the
# claude-lowering branch; subject to change.
emit Ui.*
use Ui.*

@main: @((!Nat, $Nat))
@main:
    !go <- Ui.Button($label=$"go")
    $n <- 0 then $n + 1 on !go
    @ ((($n + 1) on !go, $n))
